From b62f2f7b083e4683af2002bd2cd8479b49c9223e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:49:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/60] ppc32: ZeroExtendsWord32ToWord64NoPhis is a 64-bit-only
 selector member

G5 parade #6 (2026-10-27, same TU): instruction-selector-ppc.cc:1559
`no declaration matches bool
InstructionSelectorT::ZeroExtendsWord32ToWord64NoPhis(OpIndex)`.
instruction-selector.h declares it (with ZeroExtendsWord32ToWord64,
MarkNodeAsNotZeroExtended, Upper32BitsState, node_count_, phi_states_)
under V8_TARGET_ARCH_64_BIT only, and the generic selector calls it
from a block with the same guard.  Upstream's ppc file, PPC64-only
since 13.6, defines it unconditionally; the 32-bit selector commit
guarded visitors against the generic VISIT_UNSUPPORTED_OP list but not
against the header's 64-bit-only declarations.

Gate the definition on V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64.  Check of the class: the
three members declared under V8_TARGET_ARCH_64_BIT were matched against
every InstructionSelectorT:: definition in the ppc file outside a PPC64
region - this was the only one (the other two are defined in
instruction-selector.cc).

The two -Wreturn-type warnings on SelectLoadOpcode are not ours: both
functions end exactly as upstream's do (an exhaustive switch whose last
case is UNREACHABLE()), and gcc 16 reports the same for upstream's
MemoryRepresentation::ToMachineType in representations.h.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc b/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc
index 866f9a0..4241517 100644
--- a/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc
@@ -1556,9 +1556,12 @@ void InstructionSelectorT::VisitSignExtendWord32ToInt64(OpIndex node) {
 }
 #endif  // V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
 
+#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
+// Declared by instruction-selector.h under V8_TARGET_ARCH_64_BIT only.
 bool InstructionSelectorT::ZeroExtendsWord32ToWord64NoPhis(OpIndex node) {
   UNIMPLEMENTED();
 }
+#endif  // V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
 
 #if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
 void InstructionSelectorT::VisitChangeUint32ToUint64(OpIndex node) {
